// yq-keepwarm: a Cloudflare Worker with Cron Triggers (Workers Free plan, 24-Sep-2026) that keeps the
// Render API warm, keeps the Supabase project from pausing and runs the shop's scheduled endpoints. It
// replaces the GitHub Actions cadence: keepalive.yml says "*/10" and shop-cron.yml "*/15", but GitHub
// throttles scheduled workflows on free public repos to a median gap of ~201 min (measured 21-24 Sep), so
// the API was cold (11-12 s) in business hours, assigned orders were never chased and the 08:00 agent
// hour was mostly missed.
// keepalive.yml stays as a backstop for the Supabase 7-day pause until the repository is made private (its
// schedule is then removed, manual runs only); shop-cron.yml keeps only its manual trigger (its schedule is
// commented out - this Worker is the one scheduler, and the API's run_shop_jobs holds a 10-minute lease so a
// stray second caller is skipped, not doubled).
//
// Code: workers/keepwarm.js (no build step). Triggers, in UTC:
//   */10 * * * *      two legs, in this order, every 10 min around the clock:
//                     1. GET /health (28-Sep-2026: was 06:00-22:59 Bahrain; */15 alone sits on Render's
//                        15-min idle line).
//                     2. GET {SUPABASE_URL}/rest/v1/keepalive_ping?select=id&limit=1 with the PUBLISHABLE
//                        (anon) key as apikey + Bearer - the read keepalive.yml makes, which keeps the free
//                        project out of its 7-day pause. 200/206 = awake; the log says only
//                        "keepalive_ping -> HTTP <status>", never the body. A failed read logs an error on
//                        every tick and sends a Telegram message at most once per 6 hours, with no stored
//                        state: only the tick in the first 10 minutes of UTC hour 0, 6, 12 or 18 may send
//                        it (03:00, 09:00, 15:00, 21:00 Bahrain), so the first alert of a new outage can be
//                        up to 6 hours late.
//   */15 * * * *      GET the SCHEDULER_PATHS with X-Agent-Key (the same call shop-cron.yml makes)
// Both count as Worker invocations: ~240/day against the free 100,000/day (the Supabase and Telegram calls
// are subrequests of the 10-minute invocation). Cron Triggers are free. A third cron trigger is not needed
// and not allowed by tests/test_r1_alerts.py (it pins exactly two).
//
// RENDER FREE-HOURS BUDGET: the */15 scheduler trigger runs around the clock, so the free Render
// service never idles long enough to spin down. That is ~720-744 of the 750 free instance-hours
// per workspace per month (Render bills a free instance for the hours it is awake). It fits only
// while ONE free web service is awake in the workspace: yq-ops-api-sg (Singapore, 28-Sep-2026), with
// the old Frankfurt yq-ops-assistant SUSPENDED as the rollback (a suspended service spends no hours); a
// second free service would push the workspace over 750 h late in the month and Render suspends
// BOTH until the 1st. Options if that day comes: trim the scheduler trigger to business hours plus
// a sparse overnight one (Workers Free allows 5 cron triggers), or move the API to a paid instance.
//
// DEPLOY (from web/, needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN + CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID in the env, like deploy_cf.py):
//   npx --yes wrangler@4 deploy -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc
//   npx --yes wrangler@4 secret put AGENT_API_KEY -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc        (paste the Render value)
//   npx --yes wrangler@4 secret put SUPABASE_URL -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc         (https://<project ref>.supabase.co)
//   npx --yes wrangler@4 secret put SUPABASE_ANON_KEY -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc    (the PUBLISHABLE key, the value of
//                                                      keepalive.yml's repository secret; NEVER the service key)
//   npx --yes wrangler@4 secret put TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc   (the API's TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN on Render)
//   npx --yes wrangler@4 secret put TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc     (the API's TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID on Render)
// AGENT_API_KEY is the API's key (the value behind the X-Agent-Key header); without it the scheduler leg logs an
// error and does nothing. Without SUPABASE_URL or SUPABASE_ANON_KEY the Supabase leg logs an error naming the two
// commands on every tick and reads nothing. Without the two TELEGRAM_* secrets a failed read is logged only (one
// warning line). The health leg always runs.
// Verify: Workers & Pages -> yq-keepwarm -> Triggers shows both crons; Logs (or
// `wrangler tail -c wrangler.keepwarm.jsonc`) shows "/health -> HTTP 200" and "keepalive_ping -> HTTP 200" lines. The
// Worker has no public URL (workers_dev off, no routes) - a dashboard "Send request" answers 404 by design.
// Test the alert once: a few minutes before 09:00 or 15:00 Bahrain put a wrong value into SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (the
// secret put command above); the :00 tick logs "keepalive_ping -> HTTP 401" and the Telegram message arrives. Then
// put the real key back and confirm that the next tick logs "keepalive_ping -> HTTP 200".
{
  "name": "yq-keepwarm",
  "main": "workers/keepwarm.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-18",
  "workers_dev": false,
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  "vars": {
    "API_URL": "https://api.yqmarketplace.com",
    // Comma-separated; mirrors the loop in .github/workflows/shop-cron.yml. Trim to
    // "/scheduler/shop-jobs" if the agent reactions or the daily agents should stay on GitHub only.
    "SCHEDULER_PATHS": "/scheduler/shop-jobs,/scheduler/run-due,/events/dispatch"
  },
  "triggers": {
    "crons": ["*/10 * * * *", "*/15 * * * *"]
  }
}
